HiT — third-party components and datasets
==========================================

This repository bundles or depends on the following third-party work. Each is
used under its own license; this NOTICE documents attribution.

Code
----
* docTR (Mindee) — Apache License 2.0.
  `finetuning/train_pytorch.py`, `finetuning/utils.py`, `finetuning/evaluate_pytorch.py`
  are docTR's recognition reference scripts (from doctr v0.11.0-17-g903e9114d), included
  verbatim with their original Apache-2.0 headers. https://github.com/mindee/doctr
* olmOCR (Allen Institute for AI) — used as a rendering/prompt dependency
  (`olmocr.data.renderpdf`, `olmocr.prompts`). See its repository for license terms.

Datasets
--------
* finebooks / BHL ground truth — CC-BY 3.0.
  "IMPACT Centre of Competence & Biodiversity Heritage Library (2012). IMPACT-BHL
  ground truth (PRImA PAGE XML, CC-BY 3.0)." Hugging Face: finebooks/bhl-impact-gt.
  Redistributed here (external_datasets/finebooks/gt/) with attribution.
* Rodrigo corpus 1.0.0 — Zenodo doi:10.5281/zenodo.1490009.
  Serrano, N., Castro-Bleda, M. J., & Juan, A. "The RODRIGO Database", LREC 2010.
  Page-level GT under external_datasets/rodrigo/gt/ is reconstructed from the corpus.

Model weights
-------------
* DHiSS / DHiSS+ fine-tuned recognizers are hosted on the Hugging Face Hub
  (tsunayoshi21/HiT-DHiSS-recognizers) and fetched via ocr_weights/download.py.
